---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getSiteUrlConfig } from '../lib/site-urls';

const { urlStandard, urlMcpMarketing } = getSiteUrlConfig(import.meta.env);
---

<Layout
	title="AADM + Cursor — How they work together"
	description="AADM shapes how agents reason and what to demand. Cursor applies those standards in your workspace. Understanding the division makes both more useful."
	headerActiveNav={null}
>
	<main id="main">

		<!-- Hero -->
		<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-16 pt-16 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24">
			<p class="mb-4 inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">
				<span class="rounded-full border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/60 px-3 py-1 text-accent-violet">
					AADM + Cursor
				</span>
			</p>
			<h1 class="font-display max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold leading-[1.08] tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
				Standard as coaching.
				<span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-violet to-accent-blue bg-clip-text text-transparent">
					Cursor as editor.
				</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
				AADM defines the workflows, layer language, and evidence discipline. Cursor—and the model inside it—opens
				your project and applies that standard to real code. Understanding the division makes both more useful.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-500">
				<strong class="text-slate-400">Step 0:</strong>{' '}
				<code class="font-mono-cta text-xs text-slate-300">npx aadm-init-repo --full</code> —{' '}
				<a href="/governance" class="font-semibold text-accent-violet underline hover:text-accent-blue"
					>init guide</a
				>
			</p>
			<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
				<a
					href={urlMcpMarketing}
					class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 via-violet-600 to-blue-600 px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-violet-950/40 transition hover:brightness-110"
				>
					Connect via MCP
				</a>
				<a
					href={urlStandard}
					class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-sm transition hover:border-slate-500/40 hover:bg-surface-mid"
				>
					Read the standard
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- What AADM actually does -->
		<section class="border-y border-border-subtle bg-surface-mid/40 py-16 sm:py-20">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
				<div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-start">
					<div>
						<h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
							What AADM actually does
						</h2>
						<p class="mt-4 text-slate-400">
							AADM—the standard plus MCP—is <strong class="text-slate-300">guidance and guardrails</strong>:
							workflows (Navigator / Investigator / Sentinel), layer language, evidence-before-fix discipline,
							templates, and tools that return structured prompts and checklists.
						</p>
						<p class="mt-4 text-slate-400">
							It is <strong class="text-slate-300">not your app</strong> and does not run inside your product
							codebase.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="space-y-4">
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/90 p-6">
							<h3 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">What the MCP does not do</h3>
							<ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
								<li>
									<span class="font-semibold text-accent-violet">No repo scan</span> — the MCP server does not
									read your codebase or issue a "certified compliant" verdict.
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="font-semibold text-accent-blue">No pass/fail score</span> — real behavioral
									proof stays with your repo: tests, CI, traces, and review.
								</li>
								<li>
									<span class="font-semibold text-slate-300">No app patching</span> — AADM shapes what agents
									demand (e.g. "pair mutations with invalidation"); it doesn't patch your branch.
								</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<p class="rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-slate-600/50 bg-surface-mid/50 p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
							From the AGENTS.md positioning:{' '}
							<em class="text-slate-400">"Application repos prove AADM through code, tests, and evidence."</em>
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- What Cursor does -->
		<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
				What Cursor / the AI does
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-slate-400">
				Cursor and the model can open your project, grep, read files, and change code. That is normal
				engineering work in your workspace—not "AADM certifying" anything.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-slate-400">
				If the model ever said it violated AADM by reading code, that was an over-correction. AADM never
				says "don't read the repo." It says the MCP isn't the authority that scanned everything—and you
				shouldn't treat tool output as a compliance score without your own evidence.
			</p>

			<ul class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
				<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/80 p-6 shadow-xl shadow-black/20">
					<h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-accent-violet">Navigator</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
						<strong class="text-slate-300">Planned delivery:</strong> Cursor scopes and implements
						net-new work. AADM provides the workflow language for what "ready" looks like before
						you ship.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/80 p-6 shadow-xl shadow-black/20">
					<h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-accent-blue">Investigator</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
						<strong class="text-slate-300">Defect work:</strong> Cursor reads traces, greps code, and
						applies fixes. AADM enforces evidence-before-fix—recon first, remediation only after the
						failure is classified.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/80 p-6 shadow-xl shadow-black/20">
					<h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-violet-300">Sentinel</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
						<strong class="text-slate-300">Assurance:</strong> Cursor traces AUTH and UDALI seams across
						your codebase. AADM defines what evidence is required to attest alignment—not a vibes check.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<!-- Cursor in action (illustrative UI) -->
		<section class="border-y border-border-subtle bg-surface-deep py-16 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="cursor-in-action-heading">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
				<h2 id="cursor-in-action-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
					Cursor in action
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-slate-400">
					Illustrative UI only—the transcript is fictional. Real MCP payloads follow{' '}
					<code class="font-mono-cta text-slate-500">tools/list</code> contracts on your server build.
				</p>

				<figure
					class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-[#3e3e42] bg-[#181818] shadow-2xl shadow-black/50 ring-1 ring-white/5"
					aria-label="Fictional Cursor editor window showing chat and MCP tool calls"
				>
					<!-- Title bar -->
					<div class="flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-[#2d2d2d] bg-[#1f1f1f] px-3 py-2">
						<div class="flex gap-1.5 pl-1" aria-hidden="true">
							<span class="h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-[#ff5f57]/90"></span>
							<span class="h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-[#febc2e]/90"></span>
							<span class="h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-[#28c840]/90"></span>
						</div>
						<div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center justify-center gap-2">
							<svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-slate-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
								<path
									d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5zM2 17l10 5 10-5M2 12l10 5 10-5"
									opacity=".35"
								></path>
							</svg>
							<span class="truncate font-mono-cta text-xs text-slate-400">workspace-api — Cursor</span>
						</div>
						<span class="w-14 shrink-0"></span>
					</div>

					<div class="flex min-h-[520px] flex-col lg:min-h-[560px] lg:flex-row">
						<!-- Activity bar -->
						<div
							class="flex flex-row gap-1 border-b border-[#2d2d2d] bg-[#181818] px-2 py-2 lg:w-12 lg:flex-col lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r lg:py-3"
							aria-hidden="true"
						>
							<div class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-[#2d2d2d] text-slate-300">💬</div>
							<div class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-slate-600 opacity-60">📄</div>
							<div class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-slate-600 opacity-60">🔍</div>
						</div>

						<!-- Chat column -->
						<div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col bg-[#1e1e1e]">
							<div class="border-b border-[#2d2d2d] px-4 py-2">
								<p class="font-mono-cta text-[10px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">
									Agent · MCP enabled
								</p>
								<p class="truncate text-xs text-slate-400">Slice audit · L7 DTO / serialization · Sentinel framing</p>
							</div>

							<div class="flex-1 space-y-4 overflow-y-auto px-4 py-4 font-mono-cta text-[13px] leading-relaxed">
								<!-- User -->
								<div class="flex justify-end">
									<div class="max-w-[92%] rounded-2xl rounded-br-md bg-[#264f78] px-4 py-3 text-[#e8f1ff]">
										<p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-200/80">You</p>
										<p class="mt-1">
											Run a Sentinel-style slice on our workspace API: trace critical fields from request → schema →
											domain → DB → DTO → JSON response. Flag leakage, rename mismatches, and silent truncation—not
											just “is auth enforced.” Use AADM MCP for workflow + audit scaffolding.
										</p>
									</div>
								</div>

								<!-- Agent text -->
								<div class="flex justify-start">
									<div class="max-w-[92%] rounded-2xl rounded-bl-md border border-[#333] bg-[#252526] px-4 py-3 text-slate-300">
										<p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-violet-300/90">Agent</p>
										<p class="mt-1 text-slate-400">
											On it. I’ll pull the orchestrator snapshot, then kick an assurance-shaped audit run so we inherit
											the section spine and suggested AUTH pulls—then I’ll summarize data-flow risks for your team.
										</p>
									</div>
								</div>

								<!-- Tool: standard_brief -->
								<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-violet-500/35 bg-[#1a1625]">
									<div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-950/40 px-3 py-2">
										<span class="rounded bg-violet-600/80 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-white">MCP</span>
										<span class="text-[11px] text-violet-200/90">tools/call</span>
										<code class="text-[12px] text-emerald-300">standard_brief</code>
									</div>
									<pre class="max-h-32 overflow-y-auto p-3 text-[11px] text-slate-400">{`{
  "capabilities_schema_version": "…",
  "sentinel_assurance": { "workflow_id": "assurance", "stages": [ … ] },
  "follow_on_catalog": [ { "id": "audit_run_nl", "suggested_tool": "audit_run" }, … ]
}`}</pre>
								</div>

								<!-- Tool: audit_run -->
								<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-[#0f1a17]">
									<div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-950/35 px-3 py-2">
										<span class="rounded bg-emerald-700/90 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-white">MCP</span>
										<span class="text-[11px] text-emerald-200/80">tools/call</span>
										<code class="text-[12px] text-emerald-300">audit_run</code>
									</div>
									<pre class="max-h-36 overflow-y-auto p-3 text-[11px] text-slate-400">{`{
  "request": "Assess workspace API for response leakage, camelCase vs snake_case mismatches, date/string drift in DTOs, and silent batch truncation across adapter → service → mapper.",
  "app_name": "Workspace API (illustrative)"
}`}</pre>
								</div>

								<!-- Tool: fetch_auth -->
								<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-sky-500/25 bg-[#0f1724]">
									<div class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-sky-500/15 bg-sky-950/30 px-3 py-2">
										<span class="rounded bg-sky-700/90 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold text-white">MCP</span>
										<span class="text-[11px] text-sky-200/70">tools/call</span>
										<code class="text-[12px] text-sky-300">fetch_auth</code>
									</div>
									<pre class="p-3 text-[11px] text-slate-400">{`{ "auth_id": "AUTH-21" }  // DTO / boundary discipline (illustrative cite)`}</pre>
								</div>

								<!-- Agent long reply -->
								<div class="flex justify-start">
									<div
										class="max-w-[98%] rounded-2xl rounded-bl-md border border-[#333] bg-[#252526] px-4 py-3 text-slate-300"
									>
										<p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-violet-300/90">Agent</p>
										<p class="mt-2 text-slate-400">
											Here’s the slice readout—framed as <strong class="text-slate-200">data-flow</strong> bugs (harder
											than “is the filter present?” enforcement checks):
										</p>
										<div class="mt-3 max-h-52 overflow-y-auto rounded-lg border border-[#3e3e42] bg-[#1e1e1e] p-3 text-[12px]">
											<p class="font-semibold text-amber-200/90">Representative risks (illustrative)</p>
											<ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-4 text-slate-400">
												<li>
													<strong class="text-slate-300">Field leakage</strong> — response includes internal-only columns
													(e.g. soft-delete metadata) because the list DTO mirrors the persistence model.
												</li>
												<li>
													<strong class="text-slate-300">Format mismatch</strong> —
													<code class="text-sky-300/90">deleted_at</code> stored correctly but serialized as a plain string
													where clients expect ISO-8601—breaks downstream parsers.
												</li>
												<li>
													<strong class="text-slate-300">Silent truncation</strong> — batch accepts 100 rows; mapper drops
													half with no error surface—clients trust counts from the request, not the payload.
												</li>
											</ul>
											<p class="mt-4 text-slate-500">
												These are contract / observability problems across hops—not a substitute for gateway AUTH, which
												still has to be proven in your repo.
											</p>
											<p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-300">Trace discipline (what we’d prove in code)</p>
											<ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-4 text-slate-400">
												<li>
													Follow each critical field: UI input → API schema → domain → persistence → serialization → client
													types.
												</li>
												<li>
													At every hop ask: name alignment, type alignment, intentional transforms, inclusion/exclusion in the
													outbound contract.
												</li>
												<li>
													Compare three artifacts: frontend types, OpenAPI or response schema, and actual JSON from a live
													call—not just “mapper exists.”
												</li>
											</ol>
											<p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-300">Illustrative mismatch patterns</p>
											<dl class="mt-2 space-y-3 text-slate-400">
												<div>
													<dt class="text-slate-300">Rename drift</dt>
													<dd class="mt-1 pl-0">
														Request uses <code class="text-sky-300/90">workspaceId</code>; DB uses{' '}
														<code class="text-sky-300/90">workspace_id</code>; response accidentally emits snake_case—mobile
														clients break.
													</dd>
												</div>
												<div>
													<dt class="text-slate-300">Shape drift</dt>
													<dd class="mt-1 pl-0">
														Domain computes nested scores correctly; DTO flattens or swaps structure—validators pass while UX
														regresses.
													</dd>
												</div>
												<div>
													<dt class="text-slate-300">Null vs missing</dt>
													<dd class="mt-1 pl-0">
														<code class="text-sky-300/90">embedding: null</code> is valid JSON but callers assumed omission—
														<code class="text-sky-300/90">.length</code> crashes without a defensive read.
													</dd>
												</div>
											</dl>
											<p class="mt-4 border-t border-[#3e3e42] pt-3 text-[11px] text-slate-500">
												Next: paste the <code class="text-slate-400">coding_agent_markdown</code> brief from a real{' '}
												<code class="text-slate-400">audit_run</code> response into this thread, pair it with two HAR or test
												fixtures, and we’ll turn this into repo-specific file paths and fixes—still evidence-first.
											</p>
										</div>
									</div>
								</div>

								<!-- Composer -->
								<div class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-[#444] bg-[#252526]/80 px-3 py-2.5 text-[12px] text-slate-600">
									<span class="text-slate-500">Plan, search, build anything…</span>
									<span class="float-right text-[10px] text-slate-600">Agent ⌘I · MCP</span>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<figcaption class="border-t border-[#2d2d2d] bg-[#1f1f1f] px-4 py-2 text-center text-[11px] text-slate-500">
						Fictional transcript for storytelling — not captured from a live workspace.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Q&A table -->
		<section class="border-y border-border-subtle bg-surface-mid/40 py-16 sm:py-20">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
				<h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">Direct answers</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-slate-400">Common questions about how responsibility divides between AADM and Cursor.</p>

				<div class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/80">
					<table class="w-full text-sm">
						<thead>
							<tr class="border-b border-border-subtle">
								<th class="px-6 py-4 text-left text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Question</th>
								<th class="px-6 py-4 text-left text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Short answer</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody class="divide-y divide-border-subtle">
							<tr>
								<td class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-300 font-medium">Does AADM "do adherence"?</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-400">
									It defines adherence expectations and process. Your repo and tests demonstrate adherence.
								</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-300 font-medium">Does Cursor fix the code?</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-400">
									Yes — fixes happen in your codebase via the agent (or you). AADM doesn't patch your repo by itself.
								</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-300 font-medium">Should Cursor read the repo?</td>
								<td class="px-6 py-4 text-slate-400">
									Yes. Verifying alleged gaps with Read/grep in your repo is appropriate—claiming "no remediation needed"
									must be justified by behavior (repro, GET before/after), not line reads alone.
								</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Mental model callout -->
		<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-card/80 p-8 sm:p-10">
				<h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white sm:text-2xl">Sound mental model</h2>
				<div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:gap-8">
					<div class="flex-1 rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-mid/60 p-5">
						<p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-violet">AADM</p>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Standard + coaching. Defines what "done right" looks like and what to demand from every agent turn.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="flex-1 rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-mid/60 p-5">
						<p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-blue">Your app + CI</p>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Proof. Tests, traces, and review that confirm the branch actually does what AADM coaching demanded.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="flex-1 rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-mid/60 p-5">
						<p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-300">Cursor</p>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Editor / agent. Applies the coaching to real code in your workspace—reads, greps, and ships the fixes.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
					Model inconsistency (e.g. "gaps don't exist" from a line read, then "I shouldn't verify in code") is not a
					faithful reading of AADM. The standard asks for behavioral proof—not permission to avoid reading your repo.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
				<a
					href={urlMcpMarketing}
					class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 via-violet-600 to-blue-600 px-6 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-violet-950/40 transition hover:brightness-110"
				>
					Get MCP access
				</a>
				<a
					href="/claude-code"
